      Course setting app for the Mac
      You export your courses to your results software as an IOF XML 3.0 file, as you do from other course setting apps. The app is in development.











      Map: Kauppi, Tampereen Pyrintö



      What you need

        A Mac with macOS 14 Sonoma or later
        A map as a PDF, PNG, JPEG or TIFF file





        Ask for a beta invite
        The beta is for club course setters with a Mac. At first there is room for 10–20 course setters, so we can't promise everyone an invite.


        Email address

        That doesn't look like an email address. Please check it.






          Leave this field empty




          Email me an invite to the Ratametsuri beta and let me know when the app is released. My address won't be used for anything else or passed on. I can remove my address at any time. More about privacy: koivupiilo.fi/en/privacy

        Ask for an invite


          We sent you a confirmation email. Confirm your address with the button in it.
          Your request didn't get through. Try again in a moment.
          You can also ask for an invite by email: jarkko@koivupiilo.fi





      What Ratametsuri can already do


          1The pointer shows what a click will do
          Over another course's control, the text next to the pointer reads, for example, “Add 31 as 4”, and over a leg, “Insert between 2 and 3”. Click a control that is already on the course and the click selects it instead of adding it a second time.


          2In Finnish
          The Finnish version uses the Finnish Orienteering Federation's terms, such as “rastin­määritteet” (control descriptions) and “rasti­pisteen kohde” (control feature).


          3PDF and IOF XML 3.0
          Each course gets its own PDF with the control descriptions on the map. You can't edit columns E, G and H yet. MeOS 5.0 has imported Ratametsuri's courses without warnings. We haven't tried other results software.







